The borrowing flow in your system works in two stages based on your database schema:  Search Catalog (/student-catalog): Students search for available books and click "Request Hold". This creates a record in the holds table with a pending status.  Hold Requests (/student-holds): Students track their requested books here while waiting to pick them up from the library.  Physical Counter Pickup (Loan Creation): Students collect the physical book at the library desk, where a librarian/staff member approves and issues the transaction. Because your loans table requires an issued_by_staff_id, actual active loans are generated by library staff and then displayed under My Borrowed Books (/student-loans).  